------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. THIRD-PARTY STANDARDS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ISO/IEC 27001:2022 clause and control numbers and their short titles are
referenced for mapping purposes only. The text of the standard is not
reproduced in this package. The numbers, the titles and any description of what
a clause or control asks are excluded from the licence in section 1, including
its permission for training data and retrieval; all rights in the standard
remain with ISO and IEC. References to EU legal acts (NIS 2 Directive
(EU) 2022/2555, GDPR, CRA, the AI Act, CIR (EU) 2024/2690) follow the official
texts on EUR-Lex, (c) European Union, https://eur-lex.europa.eu, cited with
the source acknowledged (https://github.com/NISD2/open-isms/blob/main/LICENSE-DATA.md). German
statutes such as the BSIG are official works without copyright protection
(section 5(1) UrhG).

